Package: dsVert
Type: Package
Title: DataSHIELD Server-Side Functions for Vertically Partitioned Data
Version: 1.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("David", "Sarrat González", email = "david.sarrat@isglobal.org",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Miron", "Banjac", email = "miron.banjac@isglobal.org",
           role = "ctb"),
    person("Juan R", "González", email = "juanr.gonzalez@isglobal.org",
           role = "ctb")
  )
Description: Server-side DataSHIELD functions for privacy-aware analysis
    of vertically partitioned federated data. The audited remotely invocable
    surface is an exact allowlist containing only fixed-capacity pinned PSI,
    data-independent identity/schema/status replies, typed authenticated peer
    transport, server-authoritative stateless sticky Count and fixed-domain
    Frequency execution, and fixed-shape biomedical DP capsule lifecycles.
    Historical
    GLM, Cox PH, negative-binomial, multinomial, ordinal, LMM, GEE, GLMM, IPW,
    multiple-imputation and iterative-LASSO kernels remain namespace-internal
    for migration regression tests, but are neither registered nor exported.
    The promoted add/remove mechanisms use two pinned peers, exact-GC joint
    discrete-Laplace draws, fixed public clamps, bilateral signatures and
    deterministic byte-identical replay. Ring128 encrypted source transport
    prepares bounded biomedical vectors, and no vector is released before its
    joint sampler and finalizer are attested. MPC protects protocol intermediates;
    malicious-peer security and absolute non-reconstruction outside each
    documented mechanism and threat model are not claimed.
    Identity discovery can bootstrap without a logical site name, while every
    authenticated peer bind requires a persistent server-owned peer name.
